  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts, and it passes `typecheck`. I couldn't run `vite build` or load the page in a browser, so how it looks and whether it renders are untested. The scene has a 260×260 ground plane and exactly 10,000 instanced objects in three draw calls: 8,000 trunks (`instances.cylinder`), 8,000 canopies (`instances.cone`) and 2,000 rocks (`instances.sphere`). Placement comes from a fixed-seed LCG inside a 70-unit radius, so the forest is the same on every load. Canopies get a random green `hsl` colour per instance and rocks get a random grey-brown one. A single directional light casts shadows (`shadow: { mapSize: 4096 }`) and `effects.fog` provides the fog. The camera is `camera.orbit` with `autoRotate: 0.08`, starting at [0, 80, 125] and looking at [0, 2, 0], which should keep the whole forest in frame. The engine's own loop renders continuously, and `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set in the first `onFrame` callback. I'm not sure the shadow frustum covers the whole forest, because I left the directional light's shadow-fitting option at its default.",
